WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.781
AI agent logging and monitoring provide
visibility into instructions,

2
00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:13.658
context, retrieval, memory, decisions,
tool use, authorizations, actions,

3
00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:15.694
errors, and outcomes.

4
00:00:15.774 --> 00:00:22.777
Agents can read data, reason over it, call
tools, and affect downstream systems.

5
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:29.550
That means teams need traces that explain
not only what the final answer said,

6
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:35.088
but how the agent arrived there and what
happened along the way.

7
00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:41.758
Strong monitoring is privacy-aware,
evidence-focused, identity-aware,

8
00:00:41.838 --> 00:00:46.266
tool-aware, and connected to response
workflows.

9
00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:53.142
Useful logs show what happened, why it was
allowed or denied, who was involved,

10
00:00:53.222 --> 00:00:59.916
what data was accessed, what action
occurred, and what system state changed.

11
00:00:59.996 --> 00:01:06.586
They also avoid storing secrets,
credentials, unnecessary personal data,

12
00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:13.565
or full sensitive content when safer
metadata will support the investigation.

13
00:01:13.645 --> 00:01:16.426
Tool calls, retrieval, memory,

14
00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:21.552
and authorization decisions deserve
special attention.

15
00:01:21.632 --> 00:01:24.927
Tools connect agents to real systems.

16
00:01:25.007 --> 00:01:28.817
Retrieval and memory shape model behavior.

17
00:01:28.897 --> 00:01:35.796
Authorization decisions show whether
access or actions complied with policy.

18
00:01:35.876 --> 00:01:43.290
Correlation IDs and source provenance make
these events traceable across frontend,

19
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:49.034
backend, model gateway, tool services, and
downstream systems.

20
00:01:49.114 --> 00:01:53.027
The goal is not to record everything
forever.

21
00:01:53.107 --> 00:01:59.080
The goal is to capture the right evidence
for security, reliability,

22
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:04.411
accountability, governance, and continuous
improvement.

23
00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:09.743
A well-monitored agent is easier to debug,
safer to operate,

24
00:02:09.823 --> 00:02:16.516
more trustworthy for users, and more
recoverable when something goes wrong.

25
00:02:16.596 --> 00:02:22.260
Observability is part of the architecture,
not an afterthought.
